{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/458378-does-obfuscate-work-over-phone-video-feeds","id":458378,"title":"Does Obfuscate work over Phone / Video Feeds?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-03-26T15:12:34-07:00","id":458378,"title":"Does Obfuscate work over Phone / Video Feeds?","content":"This has come up in game, and I'm finding woefully little text support entirely in 2e. Is Obfuscate intended to work over the phone (only relevant with Obfuscate 4) or video feeds at all? Is there text or something to support one way or the other?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1157-soulgambit","name":"SoulGambit","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"912"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-26T23:12:20-07:00","id":458707,"title":"","content":"I gave a similar answer in the &quot;Obfuscate and Record Media&quot; thread, which you may also be interested in checking out, but here's how I see it working in respect to live audio and/or video feeds as opposed to recorded.<br /> <br /> Remember that Obfuscate does not change the actual appearance of the object, person, or place that it is being used on. It works by changing the observer's perception of the object, person, or place. It's like a form of mind control, and recording equipment is an impartial observer with no mind to control.<br /> <br /> The obfuscated subject is not invisible or disguised, so the camera or phone or what ever is objectively streaming that subject as they actually appear (assuming they don't have the lost visage active). However, the person watching or listening to the feed will not notice the subject on the screen.<br /> <br /> Maybe the security guard zones out at the wrong time, or maybe they just don't notice anything they think is suspicious and quickly forget about it. Maybe the video or sound quality is bad and the subject can't be made out clearly. Or maybe the observer is looking directly at or listening to the subject on the screen, but still don't see them because of the power altering their perception.<br /> <br /> The way it's narrated can be flexible, the important thing is, the subject is there, in plain sight, and the recording equipment is picking them up correctly. But the power causes people watching or listening to the feed simply doesn't notice the subject anyway.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-27T05:42:27-07:00","id":458828,"title":"","content":"There's also the Lost Visage (p 60 VtR 2E, dunno page reference in 1E) to consider. I feel like, as written, it should apply to live feeds, video, and the like. It doesn't explicitly say this, of course.<br /> <br /> I feel like with the Lost Visage + Obfuscate you've got a strong case for &quot;Unlikely to be noticed&quot; though I'm sure an attentive security guard or observer will at least realize that <i>something</i> is wrong.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=484226#post484226\" target=\"_blank\">Nihhina kalekal-zidu kal masun, kal manudanadu. Nihhina kalekal-zidu nukal shaghu-desasudu \u2014 nihhina kalekal-zidu kal innu-desasudu udhkal samm</a>.&quot; Arthur Ashe<br /> She/her, contributing writer for <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/363404/Scion-Pride-2021\" target=\"_blank\">Scion: Pride 2021</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1923-bigdamnhero","name":"BigDamnHero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1923_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1263"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-27T07:26:51-07:00","id":458988,"title":"","content":"Phone and audio recordings are the most relevant to my immediate situation, which the Lost Visage doesn't apply to (I don't think?). Specifically trying to see if using Obfuscate 4 to impersonate someone over the phone is a thing. Sadly, there's absolutely no information about how Obfuscate interacts with technology.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1157-soulgambit","name":"SoulGambit","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"912"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-27T08:20:23-07:00","id":459020,"title":"","content":"I'm pretty sure Lost Visage does apply to live video feeds, but it does not apply to audio, live or recorded - it hides the vampire's image, not their voice.<br /> <br /> As for using Obfuscate 4 to disguise your voice over the phone, I don't see any reason it shouldn't work. They <i>think</i> they're hearing the voice of who ever the obfuscate user is imitating.<br /> <br /> Obfuscate doesn't interact with techchnology, any more than it interacts with air molecules or photons. What obfuscate does is alter the observer's perceptions of the subject - the way their brain interprets the information it recieves from their eyes and ears about them. The technology is simply the medium that transmits that information from the subject to the observer. It doesn't alter the information, and the Discipline doesn't alter the way the technology recieves or delivers that information. It only changes the way the observer interprets it when it gets to them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-28T06:43:36-07:00","id":459881,"title":"","content":"I always imagined that Obfuscate would &quot;work on technology&quot;, but only if the vampire, the victim, and the tech are all within line-of-sight*. In other words, if the vampire is close enough to affect you with Obfuscate, they'll affect you no matter how you're trying to perceive them- for example, a guard can't get all They Live with a cellphone camera, but they can spot an obfuscated shoplifter over a CCTV feed.<br /> <br /> It'd make a perfectly appropriate Devotion, though.<br /> <br /> *I use LOS as a term of convenience; conceptually it's more about availability than distance.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1289-hastur00","name":"Hastur00","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1289_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"366"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-28T08:23:43-07:00","id":460026,"title":"","content":"I'd personally rule it as them only being effected if Line of Effect. However, the Lost Visage will stop anyone from identifying the vampire unless they know them well enough to recognise them from the back of their head (Wits+Composure roll, with a -3 penalty for a casual acquaintance).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:blue\">Blue is sarcasm.</span><br /> <br /> If I suggestion I make contradicts in-setting metaphysics please ignore me, I probably brought in scientific ideas.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4507-twodsix","name":"TwoDSix","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"833"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}